\p
\v 10 And¦46167 they said¦46168: Listen, we've¦46195 sent you¦46172 money¦46173; therefore buy¦46175 with the¦46176 money¦46177 burnt¦46178 offerings¦46178, sin¦46181 offerings, and¦46182 incense, and¦46184 prepare¦46185 an oblation, and¦46187 offer on¦46189 the¦46190 altar¦46191 of¦46193 the¦46193 master our god¦46194;
\v 11 and¦46196 pray for the¦46199 life¦46200 of Nevukadnetsar king¦46202 of Bavel, and¦46204 for the life¦46206 of Belshatsar \add !(Belshazzar)\add* his son¦46208, that¦46210 their days may be¦46211\f + \fr 1:11 \ft See Deuteronomy 11:21.\f* as the days of¦46218 heaven¦46219 above the¦46221 earth¦46222.
\v 12 The master will give¦46224 us strength¦46226 and¦46228 light to¦46229 our eyes¦46231. We'll¦46232 live under¦46235 the¦46236 shadow¦46237 of Nevukadnetsar king¦46239 of Bavel and¦46241 under¦46242 the¦46243 shadow¦46244 of Belshatsar his son¦46246, and¦46248 we'll serve them many days¦46251, and¦46253 find¦46254 favour in¦46256 their sight.
\v 13 Pray for us also¦46258 to¦46262 the¦46264 master our god¦46265, for we've¦46266 sinned against the¦46269 master our god¦46271. To this day¦46287 the anger of the master and his indignation isn't turned from us.
