\v 3 that we¦46545 should each eat the flesh¦46547 of our own son¦46548, and¦46550 each eat the flesh¦46552 of our own daughter¦46553.
\v 4 Moreover he's given¦46556 them to be in subjection to all¦46559 the¦46560 kingdoms that¦46562 are around us, to be a reproach¦46566 and¦46567 a desolation among¦46569 all¦46570 the¦46571 people¦46572 around us, where the¦46573 master has scattered them.
\v 5 Thus they were¦46581 thrown down and¦46583 not exalted, because¦46586 we¦46590 sinned against the¦46592 master our god¦46589 in not¦46593 listening¦46594 to¦46594 his voice¦46596.
\v 6 To the¦46598 master our god¦46600 belongs righteousness¦46603, but¦46605 to us and¦46606 to our fathers¦46608 confusion of face¦46613, as at this¦46615 day¦46616.
\v 7 All¦46623 these \add ≈deadly diseases\add* have come¦46628 onto us which the master has pronounced against¦46629 us.
\v 8 Yet we haven't asked for the¦46634 favour of¦46637 the¦46637 master by everyone turning from¦46640 the thoughts of his wicked¦46647 heart¦46644.
\v 9 Therefore the master has kept¦46649 watch¦46649 over the \add ≈deadly diseases\add*. The master has brought them onto us, because¦46659 the¦46661 master is righteous in all¦46664 his works¦46666 which¦46668 he's¦46667 commanded us.
\v 10 Yet we haven't listened to¦46673 his voice¦46675, to¦46677 walk in the¦46678 master's commandments that¦46681 he's¦46676 set before us.
\s1 A prayer for mercy
\p
\v 11 And¦46686 now¦46687, Oh master, you God¦46690 of Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add* who've¦46694 brought your people¦46695 out¦46697 of the land¦46698 of Mitsrayim \add !(Egypt)\add* with a mighty hand¦46701, with signs¦46705, with wonders¦46708, with great¦46712 power¦46711, and¦46713 with a high arm¦46715, and¦46717 have gotten yourself¦46719 a name¦46720, as at this¦46722 day¦46723:
\v 12 Oh master our god¦46730, we've sinned. We've been ungodly. We've done wrong in all¦46733 your ordinances.
\v 13 Let your anger¦46739 turn from¦46741 us, for we're¦46742 but a few¦46745 left among¦46746 the¦46747 heathen where you've scattered us.
\v 14 Hear our prayer¦46756, Oh master, and¦46758 our petition¦46760, and¦46762 deliver us for¦46765 your own sake. Give¦46768 us favour in the sight of¦46770 those who've¦46773 led us away captive,
\v 15 that¦46776 all¦46778 the¦46779 earth¦46780 may know¦46777 that¦46781 you're¦46782 the¦46784 master our god¦46785, because¦46787 Yisrael and¦46794 his posterity is called¦46791 by your¦46798 name.
