\v 22 But¦46940 if¦46941 you won't¦46942 hear¦46943 the¦46944 master's voice¦46945 to serve the¦46948 king¦46949 of Bavel,
\v 23 I'll cause¦46952 to¦46952 cease out¦46953 of the cities¦46954 of Yehudah \add !(Judah)\add* and¦46956 from the region near Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add* the voice¦46959 of mirth¦46960, the voice¦46962 of gladness, voice¦46964 of the bridegroom¦46965, and¦46966 the voice¦46967 of the bride¦46968. The¦46972 whole¦46971 land¦46973 will be desolate without inhabitant.’ ”
\v 24 But¦46978 we wouldn't listen¦46980 to¦46980 your voice¦46982, to serve the¦46985 king¦46986 of Bavel. Therefore you've¦46992 made good your words¦46991 that you¦46999 spoke by your servants the¦47000 prophets¦47001, that the bones of our kings¦47006 and¦47008 the bones of our fathers¦47012 would be taken out¦47014 of¦47015 their places¦47016.
\v 25 Listen, they're¦47020 thrown out to¦47020 the heat by day¦47025 and¦47026 to the frost by night¦47030. They died in great miseries by famine, by sword¦47040, and¦47041 by\f + \fr 2:25 \ft See Yirmeyah/Jeremiah 32:36.\f* pestilence.
\v 26 You've made the¦47046 house¦47047 that's¦47048 called¦47049 by your name as it's today because¦47059 of¦47059 the wickedness¦47060 of the house¦47061 of Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add* and¦47063 the house¦47064 of Yehudah.
\s1 God's promise to bring his people home
\p
\v 27 Yet, Oh master our god¦47072, you have dealt with us after all your kindness and¦47078 according¦47079 to¦47079 all¦47080 your great¦47084 mercy,
\v 28 as¦47085 you¦47090 spoke¦47104 by your servant Mosheh \add !(Moses)\add* in¦47092 the day¦47093 when you¦47095 commanded him to¦47097 write¦47097 your law¦47099 in¦47101 the presence¦47101 of¦47101 the children¦47089 of Yisrael, saying,
\v 29 “If¦47105 you won't¦47106 hear¦47107 my voice¦47109, surely¦47111 this very¦47118 great¦47116 multitude will be turned¦47120 into a small¦47122 number among¦47123 the¦47124 nations¦47125 where I'll scatter them.
\v 30 Because¦47130 I know¦47131 that¦47132 they won't¦47134 listen¦47135 to¦47135 me, because¦47137 they're a¦47138 stiff-necked¦47139 people; but¦47141 in¦47146 the land¦47147 of their captivity they'll take it¦47149 to¦47143 heart¦47144,
